| C15 IDR | Endofunctions on four labels; replace `f(i)` by the indegree of `i` modulo four. | 256 states: image 32, three fixed points, tail 3; larger pilot already develops a two-cycle and longer tail. | **KILL.** Inventory map is unstable across size and has no sharp family theorem. |
| C16 HJP | Endofunctions; send `i` forward `1+indeg(f(i))` iterates of `f`. | 256 states: image 88, 53 fixed points, four two-cycles, tail 2. | **KILL.** State-dependent functional powering; generic power-map mechanism and no fibre axis. |
| C17 RPJ | Endofunctions; send `i` forward `1+indeg(i)` iterates of `f`. | 256 states: image 124, 113 fixed points, four two-cycles, tail 2. | **KILL.** Same power-map collision as C16, with weak temporal signal. |
| C18 CEP | Endofunctions; map each vertex to the least-labelled point on the eventual directed cycle it enters. | 256 states: image=fixed set 41, tail 1. | **KILL.** Idempotent canonical projection; no independent time theorem. |
| C19 DDP | Simple graphs; retain exactly edges whose endpoint degrees disagree. | Five vertices: image 321, 186 fixed points, tail 3.  Through six vertices the maximum tail is `n-2`. | **KILL.** The tempting clock lacks a clean arbitrary-target inverse: preimages require a coupled degree-realisation problem. |
| C20 OTP | Simple graphs; retain an edge iff it lies in an odd number of triangles. | Five vertices: image 64, 37 fixed points, tail 2. | **KILL.** Parity-neighbourhood algebra with no clean all-size clock/fibre pair. |
| C21 CNT | Simple graphs; toggle each pair having an odd number of common neighbours. | Five vertices appears convergent with tail 4; six vertices already has periods 2 and 4. | **KILL.** Early convergence was a small-size mirage; matrix-parity collision. |
| C22 EDC | Simple graphs; output all pairs whose old degrees are equal. | Five vertices: image 51, 16 fixed points, tail 2. | **KILL.** Degree-inventory classifier; arbitrary-target recovery is graph-realisation coupling. |
| C23 CCM | Simple graphs; join pairs whose closed-neighbourhood intersection is a strict majority of the smaller closed neighbourhood. | Five vertices: 574 of 1024 states fixed, tail 2. | **KILL.** Near-identity local closure, weak time and no fibre theorem. |
